    {
      "route": "/api/academy-certificates",
      "method": "POST",
      "previousSourceHash": "aad0177e0076b444ac3fc33b",
      "issue": "#109",
      "owner": "academy-platform",
      "reason": "Learning OS write contract restoration (audit findings F-13 and F-14). recordLearningEvent omitted workspace_id/principal_type/principal_id, which learning_events has required and NOT NULL since the tenant-principal migration, so every insert threw and these routes answered 500 for every event. The writer now supplies the full identity and takes workspaceId as a required argument, so each route passes tenantContext.workspaceId — that threading is the whole source change here. No control moved: the tenant and principal were already resolved from verified context at each call site, they simply were not being written. Proven by src/tests/security/learning-os-write-contract-postgres.test.ts, which drives the real writers against a migrated database.",
      "replacement": {
        "route": "/api/academy-certificates",
